ut of bounds: the len is 19 but the index is 19", "fixed_commit": "b9c57c278742e095889c2ee1354c3efbd3eb7274", "fixed_tree": "ae6aeb1f0d3a963e950f740b1c2ecd5c80cd1759", "fixes": [{"commit": "b9c57c278742e095889c2ee1354c3efbd3eb7274", "parent": "a8e2a7add93a4856758ece70429753ff8ad2b3ab"}], "patch": "patches/b9c57c278742e095889c2ee1354c3efbd3eb7274-1/20260923T231330Z-22fac92c.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "b9c57c278742e095889c2ee1354c3efbd3eb7274", "paths": ["src/lib.rs"]}], "tests": ["tests::test_label_resolution"]}, "shard": "encoding_rs", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Make overlong bogus labels not panic.", "summary": "Encoding::for_label checked whether trimmed_pos exceeded its 19-byte buffer length after writing each byte. At position 19 the check remained false, so a twentieth byte caused an out-of-bounds panic. The fix changes both checks from > to ==, returning None before another write. The regression test added by the fix exercises this with bogusbogusbogusbogus. This is a proposed reversal; no tests were run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:13:54.327228+00:00"}
